  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Overview
    
    A subterranean refuge comprising three connected caverns in The Berg's deepest accessible reaches, established during the Faction Wars as a sanctuary for Nightshelf exiles and surface-dwellers displaced by the Corpse Current. Control has passed — violently, repeatedly — among the Midnight Claws (the now-dissolved Nightshelf syndicate), the ☽'shadow Covens' Order, and the Communion (elt-sworn), a cult whose relationship with the site's deepening corruption appears less incidental than their priests acknowledge.
    
    ## Physical Condition
    
    Bioluminescent fungi struggle under accumulated soot. The walls weep dark water. Fire-cores in corroded braziers burn at uneven heights — the Communion calls this liturgical; the Midnight Claws' graffiti on the eastern wall suggests neglect. Grandmother Deep's original bone-crown settlement markers sit cracked alongside newer territorial carvings, the Shadow Covens' sigil cut deepest into the northern pillar. Migrants occupy the outer chamber where cold seeps in; those with leverage nest deeper, where the ice holds older impressions and the pressure becomes physically oppressive.
    
    The wall-maps have begun contradicting themselves — passages sealing and reopening without explanation. Ice∴freeze corruption is documented here. Several Nightshelf abilities — Drift-coalesce, ☽'glacial Crystalline~ Spiral, Hush☽ Twilight, Shawl☽ Sun — manifest within the caverns, which suggests either convergent magical instability or deliberate cultivation. I suspect the latter but cannot confirm it from the ice alone.
    
    ## The Third Cavern
    
    The quarters of ☽'Iarlocias the Silent were sealed here with bone-and-cord knots encoding *forgotten on purpose* — a Nightshelf designation I have encountered in exactly three other contexts, none of them trivial. The seals rotted through. Lector ☽'Ilsancuia subsequently recovered a dangerous aurora-glass Medallion from the unsealed nest, initiating a chain of events that fractured the Communion and killed ☽'Ilsancuia.
    
    The eastern section houses a deep-archive annex where Keeper-Registrar ☽'noctmuluevus 'born catalogues artifacts held under Pactum∴silenti covenant-bind, including three items — the ☽'micseleia' Dagger, Veil☽ Sasvaeumis~, and the Swaleed~ Luminary — all bearing damage from the Orca Incursion that resists repair.
