  annotation "note_1771582693987_0", anchor: "Grandmother Deep's original bone-crown settlement markers sit cracked alongside newer territorial carvings", text: "Grandmother Deep guides Wake-Singer theology at the Corpse Current. Her bone-crown markers in a site the Communion controls. In my Communion annotation I wrote that two unrelated cults performed blood-rites at the same crystalline structure and no one — myself included — had connected them. Here is the connection. These are not two cults. These are two names for a single network of sites, and the bone-crowns are wayfinding markers, not settlement claims. The Wake-Singers were here first. The Communion inherited their infrastructure and called it theology.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771582693987_1", anchor: "forgotten on purpose", text: "The other three: the sealed annex beneath the Whisper Galleries, one stratum of the Foundation Depths I am not at liberty to identify, and a Courier Corps dead-drop whose designation I found in administrative ice that should not have contained it. All four sites share a characteristic — the knot-encoding does not merely say *do not open* but *do not remember that this exists*. The Nightshelf distinction matters. Secrecy preserves knowledge in fewer hands. This erases it from all of them.", type: :pedantic, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771582693987_2", anchor: "killed ☽'Ilsancuia", text: "Their cracked fire-core hammer is a memorial artifact. Their guild endorsement is still in print. The Medallion started it. The chain had more links than this sentence holds, but today I am too tired to lay them all out again.", type: :correction, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771582693987_3", anchor: "I suspect the latter but cannot confirm it from the ice alone", text: "Four distinct Nightshelf abilities manifesting in the same cavern system. The probability of convergent instability producing exactly the suite a shadow-coven would cultivate — concealment, crystalline memory-work, glacial offense, and aurora-dampening — is the kind of coincidence only someone who has never read a Nightshelf operational inventory would accept.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
